    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d702">

                <pb facs="0524" n="520" xml:id="pg520"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/14248: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Canton</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Linnell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Canton</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-10-30T23:00:00+08:00">October 30, 1938—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 30—1:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>34. The British Consul General has just informed me that all the Americans
                    finally decided to remain at Wuchow. The <hi rendition="#italic">Robin</hi>
                    started for Canton but the Japanese authorities have just notified the British
                    Consul General that Japanese advance forces have seized Samshui in order to cut
                    off all communication between Canton and Wuchow and they feared an incident if
                    the <hi rendition="#italic">Robin</hi> insisted on passing Samshui. The <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Robin</hi> has been instructed to await instructions at
                    least 5 miles above Samshui.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Chungking, Peiping, and Hong Kong.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Linnell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
